 "title": "the P58 park, fourteen minutes: too precise, too slidy, slowed when not asked",
 "human": {
  "said": [
   "plugged, i think its just to precise for a human to do. maybe long jump should be down in running where you can see the do extending to judge it correctly, and the jump be on press no release. the slide can be the special button, superman punch on jab during running too. it looks cool but its too slidy i should feel more snappy to the ground, also the wall jump get annoying at times when the goal is straight ahead. no yet the fun i want.",
   "the obstacle sizes are fine its the player physics and that need calibration",
   "it should just feel a bit more like controlled parkour and be able to be run without the slow mo, slow mo is more of just for extra precision. maybe we have to rethink the controls",
   "the camera must compensate for the lack of analog control."
  ],
  "said_on": "2026-11-23",
  "knobs_chosen": []
 },
